            <ArticleTitle>Regulation of heterotrimeric G protein signaling in airway smooth muscle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heterotrimeric G proteins transduce signals from G protein-coupled receptors to regulate numerous signaling events and functions in airway smooth muscle (ASM). In this article, we detail the function and regulation of heterotrimeric G protein signaling in ASM. We further discuss recent advances in the development of experimental tools in the study of G protein signaling, and speculate how these tools might be used in therapeutic strategies that seek to mitigate bronchospasm and airway remodeling that occur in obstructive airway disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
